MODIFIED MODEL FILE: best.pt

The DriftOps team modified this model through component-specific fine-tuning
in September 2026. This file is not an unchanged upstream model release.

The model starts from google/gemma-3-270m at revision
9b0cfec892e2bc2afd938c98eabe4e4a7b1e0ca1 and the OpenTSLM temporal checkpoint
OpenTSLM/gemma-3-270m-tsqa-sp at revision
c97bd36131e07d53a7af9cd307eb3db628f9712f.

Fine-tuning updates the time-series encoder, projector, and rank-8 attention
LoRA parameters. The underlying Gemma parameters remain frozen during training.
The saved checkpoint also contains Gemma embedding and language-head tensors.

The run manifest and selection.json identify this artifact's component,
training configuration, selected epoch, and original SHA-256 checksum.
The release preserves the selected best.pt bytes and checksum.
This accompanying notice records the modification without rewriting the binary.

The model describes weak numerical pattern targets. It does not establish
fault detection, failure probability, remaining useful life, or maintenance benefit.

Gemma Terms of Use: https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms
Gemma Prohibited Use Policy: https://ai.google.dev/gemma/prohibited_use_policy
